  "id": "KP17Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Non-surgical nasal fracture treatment",
  "description": "Non-surgical nasal fracture treatment is an outpatient procedure where your doctor treats your broken nose without surgery. Nasal fractures are very common and many heal well without surgery. Your doctor will take X-rays or CT (computed tomography) scans to determine the fracture location and severity. If your nasal passages are not significantly blocked and your appearance is acceptable to you, surgery may not be needed. Treatment focuses on managing pain and swelling with ice, pain medication, and elevation. You should avoid blowing your nose and protect your face from further injury. Your doctor will monitor your healing. Once initial swelling subsides, you and your doctor can discuss whether the appearance or function warrants later surgical correction. Some nasal fractures are manipulated to improve alignment or function before healing begins. The cost of this procedure may vary depending on whether your doctor needs to manually reposition (manipulate) the bone fragments into proper alignment, or whether the fracture can heal in its current position without manipulation.",
